  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_CHOICE_SIDE_BY_SIDE' => 'Side by Side',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_REQUIRED_INDICATION' => 'Required Field Indication',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_REQUIRED_INDICATION_DESC' => 'Indicate required fields with an asterisk next to each field label. It requires the field label to not be hidden.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_INPUT_MASK' => 'Input Mask',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_INPUT_MASK_DESC' => 'Help user with the input by ensuring a predefined format. <br><br><b>Syntax:</b><br>9: Numeric (0-9)<br>a: Alphabetical (a-z or A-Z)<br>A: Uppercase alphabetical (A-Z)<br>*: Alphanumeric (0-9, a-z, or A-Z)<br>&: Uppercase alphanumeric (0-9 or A-Z)<br><br><b>Examples</b>:<br>Phone: +1 (999)-9999<br>Date: 99/99/9999<br>Zip Code: 99999?-9999',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_LEAD_USER_SUBMITTED_DATA' => 'User Submitted Data',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_NO_SUBMITTED_DATA' => 'No submitted data found',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_LEAD_INFO' => 'Submission Details',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_SUBMISSION_ENV' => 'Submission Environment',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_INTERNAL_NOTES' => 'Internal Notes',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_NOTES' => 'Submission Notes',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_NOTES_HINT' => 'Add notes about this submission — follow-ups, context, anything useful for the team...',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_STORE_IP' => 'Store IP Addresses',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_STORE_IP_DESC' => 'When enabled, the visitor\'s IP address is stored alongside each form submission. Disable this if your privacy policy requires you not to store IP addresses.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_DATE_RANGE' => 'Date Range',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_START_DATE' => 'Start Date',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_END_DATE' => 'End Date',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PERIOD' => 'Period',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PERIOD_SELECT' => '- Select Period -',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_HONEYPOT' => 'Honeypot Protection',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_HONEYPOT_DESC' => 'The Honeypot technique helps prevent spam by adding a hidden field to the form that human users cannot see or interact with. Bots, however, often fill out all fields, including the hidden one, which allows to detect and block them.<br><br><b>Honeypot v1</b>: Uses a fixed hidden field name to catch spam bots. While effective, some advanced bots may recognize and bypass it.<br><br><b>Honeypot v2</b>: Uses a dynamically generated field with a unique name for each session, making it harder for bots to detect. This version also works seamlessly with caching mechanisms, ensuring reliable spam protection on cached pages.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FIELD_FILEUPLOAD' => 'File Upload',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FIELD_FILEUPLOAD_DESC' => 'Give the user the ability to upload files',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_TEMP_FOLDER_NOT_WRITABLE' => 'Your site\'s temp folder is set to <b>%s</b> but it\'s not writable. Please specify a writable temp folder.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_FOLDER_TYPE' => 'Folder',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_STORAGE' => 'Storage',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_STORAGE_DESC' => 'Where uploaded files are kept.<br><br><b>Public</b> stores them inside your site, so anyone holding the link can open the file directly.<br><br><b>Private</b> stores them outside your site, where the web server cannot serve them at all, and delivers them through an expiring download link that you can restrict to logged-in users. It needs an Uploads Base Path set in Convert Forms Options, under Security.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_STORAGE_PUBLIC' => 'Public (direct file link)',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_STORAGE_PRIVATE' => 'Private (secure download link)',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_FOLDER_TYPE_DESC' => 'Which folder the files go to within the storage you chose above.<br><br><b>Auto</b>: Convert Forms picks the folder. Public uploads go to /media/com_convertforms/uploads, private uploads to a folder named after the form inside your Uploads Base Path. A random prefix is also added to each file name to increase security.<br><br><b>Custom</b>: Specify a destination folder and naming convention of your own, relative to your site root for Public storage or to your Uploads Base Path for Private.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_EXTERNAL_SUBFOLDER' => 'Subfolder',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_EXTERNAL_SUBFOLDER_DESC' => 'Where to store the files within the Uploads Base Path, for example applications/{year}/{month}. Smart Tags work here exactly as they do for a custom in-site destination, and the uploaded file name is added automatically. Leave empty to store the files directly in the base folder.<br><br>Set the Uploads Base Path itself in Convert Forms Options, under Security.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_DOWNLOAD_ACCESS' => 'Download Access',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_DOWNLOAD_ACCESS_DESC' => 'Who may open the download link. Public means anyone holding the link, which is how a notification email normally works. Any other level asks the visitor to log in and checks that their account has that level.<br><br>This applies only to files stored outside the site, because those are the only ones served by Convert Forms. Files kept inside the site are served directly by the web server, so they cannot be restricted this way.<br><br>The link is what this field\'s Smart Tag resolves to, so it travels anywhere you use that tag: notification emails, webhooks, API responses and exports. Files sent as real email attachments are not covered, since the file is in the message itself rather than behind a link.<br><br>Changing this takes effect immediately, including for links already sent.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_EXTERNAL_NOT_CONFIGURED' => 'Uploads cannot be stored outside the site yet: no Uploads Base Path is set. Until one is, this field will refuse uploads rather than fall back to a folder inside your site.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_EXTERNAL_NOT_CONFIGURED_LINK' => 'Set it in Options, under Security.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_INVALID_DESTINATION' => 'The upload destination is not valid.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_DOWNLOAD_LINK_INVALID' => 'This download link is not valid.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_DOWNLOAD_LINK_EXPIRED' => 'This download link has expired. Please ask for a new one.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_FOLDER' => 'Custom Folder',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_FOLDER_DESC' => 'Enter the path relative to the root of your webspace where the uploaded files will be stored. To rename uploaded files use the following Smart Tags.<br><br><b>{file.basename}</b>: cat.jpg<br><b>{file.extension}</b>: jpg<br><b>{file.filename}</b>: cat<b><br>{file.index}</b>: index number<br><br>It can also accept global Smart Tags like {year}, {month}, {user.id} or {randomid} to create an even more dynamic upload destination. Submission Smart Tags such as {submission.id} are supported too: the file is moved into its final folder right after the submission is saved, so you can group every upload under a per-submission folder like /media/com_convertforms/submissions/{submission.id}.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_LIMIT_FILES' => 'Files Limit',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_LIMIT_FILES_DESC' => 'How many files can be uploaded? Enter 0 for no limit.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_MAX_FILE_SIZE' => 'File Size Limit',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_MAX_FILE_SIZE_DESC' => 'Configure the maximum allowable size for each uploaded file in megabytes. Enter 0 for no limit. <br><br>Your server\'s maximum upload size is: <b>%s</b>.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_UPLOAD_TYPES' => 'Allowed File Types',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_UPLOAD_TYPES_DESC' => 'Enter comma separated list of allowed file types like: </b>.jpg, .gif, .png, .pdf<br><br>You may enter media types like: application/pdf, images/*, video/* or you can mix both: application/*, .png, .jpg<br><br>Note: This is not fool-proof and can be tricked, please remember that there is always a danger in allowing users to upload files.<br><br>The PHP extension <b>fileinfo</b> is required to be installed to guess the type of the file.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_EMPTY_FILE_TYPES_NOT_ALLOWED' => 'The Allowed File Types field cannot be left blank. Please specify at least one valid file extension.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FILEUPLOAD_EMPTY_FILE_EXTENSION_NOT_ALLOWED' => 'An empty extension is not allowed in the Allowed File Types. Please specify a valid file extension.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FIELD_FILTER' => 'Filter',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_FIELD_FILTER_DESC' => 'Filter the user input based on the following filters.<br><b>Text</b>: Converts the input to a plain text string; strips all tags / attributes.<br><b>Safe HTML</b>: Accept only safe HTML elements like.<br><b>Alpha Numeric</b>: Allow a-z and 0-9 only<br><b>Word</b>: Only allow characters a-z, and underscores<br><b>Integer</b>: Only use the first number value<br><b>Float</b>: Only allow characters a-z, and underscores',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_ERROR' => 'Invalid form or field key',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_ERROR_INVALID_FIELD' => 'Invalid upload field',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_ERROR_INVALID_FILE' => 'Invalid or unsupported file',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_MAX_FILES_LIMIT' => 'You can upload up to %d files',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_FILE_IS_MISSING' => 'Temporary file %s is missing. Please re-upload.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_FOLDER_INVALID' => 'The upload folder %s doesn\'t exist or is not writable',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_FILETOOBIG' => 'File is too big ({{filesize}}MB). Max filesize: {{maxFilesize}}MB.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_INVALID_FILE' => 'You can\'t upload files of this type.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_FALLBACK_MESSAGE' => 'Your browser does not support drag\'n\'drop file uploads.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_RESPONSE_ERROR' => 'Server responded with {{statusCode}} code.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_CANCEL_UPLOAD' => 'Cancel upload',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_CANCEL_UPLOAD_CONFIRMATION' => 'Are you sure you want to cancel this upload?',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_REMOVE_FILE' => 'Remove file',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_MAX_FILES_EXCEEDED' => 'You can not upload any more files.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_AUTO_DELETE' => 'Auto Delete Files',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_UPLOAD_AUTO_DELETE_DESC' => 'If you are getting a lot of uploads, the server space used by the uploaded files can quickly mount up, requiring some regular housekeeping to free up space. <br><br>This option helps you auto-delete files stored in the Upload Folder after a set period. <br><br>For example, enter 3, to auto-delete files more than 3 days old or 0 if you want to keep the files forever.<br><br>Note: The Convert Forms Uploaded Files Cleaner plugin needs to be enabled and the respective Cron Job URL set on your server.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_READONLY' => 'Read-only',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_READONLY_DESC' => 'Prevent entry into this field',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT' => 'PHP Scripts',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_FORM_DISPLAY' => 'Form Display',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_FORM_DISPLAY_DESC' => 'The PHP script added in this area is executed just before the form is displayed.<br><br>The main focus in this area is the <b>$formLayout</b> (String) variable which contains the HTML code of the form.<br><br>To access the form settings use the <b>$form</b> (Array) variable.<br><br>You don\'t need to include the &lt;?php and ?> tags.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_FORM_PROCESS' => 'Form Process',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_FORM_PROCESS_DESC' => 'The PHP code added in this area is executed just before the form data has been saved into the database regardless if the submission is valid or not. <br><br>This area is rather useful when you need to process calculations, make advanced validation or modify the value of a field. Any modifications to <b>$post</b> (Array) variable performed here, will be reflected in the submission entry.<br><br>To access the form settings use the <b>$form</b> (Array) variable. <br><br>You don\'t need to include the &lt;?php and ?> tags.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_AFTER_FORM_SUBMISSION' => 'After Form Submission',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_AFTER_FORM_SUBMISSION_DESC' => 'The PHP code added in this area is executed after the form has been successfully submitted and the data has been saved into the database. <br><br>This is rather useful when you are trying to run some extra tasks such as silently post data to another URL. You can access the final submission using the <b>$submission</b> (Object) variable.<br><br>To access the form settings use the <b>$form</b> (Array) variable. <br><br>You don\'t need to include the &lt;?php and ?> tags.',
  'COM_CONVERTFORMS_PHPSCRIPT_NOTE' => 'PHP Scripts are not executed on the backend to prevent issues with the live form previewer. Always test on the front-end.',
